  "body": "Closes #1252\nClaim: cloud/m4q-small-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/m4q-small-sonnet)\n\n**Problem.** A `// Port of … @ <sha>` pointer whose sha moved without its lines (AGENTS §2) is caught only by a later review (#1197: `AppIconSettingsView.swift:4`).\n\n**Cause.** Nothing reads the cited lines.\n\n**Change.** `tooling/docs/check_legacy_pointers.py` reads the leading `//` blocks of `App/**/*.swift`; for each `Port of <path> (<items>) @ <sha>` item of the shape `Symbol :a-b` / `Symbol a-b` / `<Symbol>, lines a-b` it checks the symbol is in lines a-b of `git show <sha>:<path>` (whole word; a range past the end is wrong). Everything else (no range, another file's range, unreadable sha, `///`) is counted unchecked and never fails. New step in **Docs consistency** (`--fetch` = `git fetch origin legacy/duo-inner-cover`); README section in `tooling/docs/README.md`. On the repository today: 24 pointers checked, 403 unchecked; the two real misses are fixed in this PR (`ComposerHeader.swift:3` and `FloatingComposerButtons.swift:4` cited `composerHeader` at 768-819, declared at 765 → 765-819; comment-only change in `App/`). The same range appears in `docs/lots/LOT-174` and `ReplyComposerView.swift:11`, which are other formats, not read yet.\n\n**Tests.** `scripts/tests/test_check_legacy_pointers.py` (6 tests, Fixture tooling job): the `AppIconSettingsView` pointer as before #1197 (`lines 360-365`) is wrong, the corrected `411-416, applyIconSelection 221-231` passes (on a stand-in legacy file); wrapped headers, a range past the end, and the never-fail cases; plus a run on the real headers. Fails without the script (import error).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
