   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, reviewer chore/1252 round 2) : REQUEST CHANGES** — head 6a63429\n\n1. **High** — `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/Seasons/SeasonalDecorations.swift:4`: the rewritten pointer line is 154 characters. `.swiftlint.yml` warns at 140 and CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict`. Running `swiftlint lint --strict` on the file gives `4:1: error: Line Length Violation … 154 characters`, so the SwiftLint job fails. It is the only line over 140 under `App/`. Fix: wrap the line. The content is correct: `setTheme` starts at 363 @ 87fe0d1c and the snow block is at 382-388.\n2. **Detail** — `tooling/docs/README.md` says \"the symbol (last component of `A.b`)\". In fact `Class.method :1-2` is left unchecked when the last component is not camelCase or PascalCase (`CODE_LIKE`), unless it is in backticks. Fix: say so in the README.\n3. **Detail** — `check_legacy_pointers.py` `SHA`: a header `(x :1-2) @ 2440d79 and @ 87fe0d1c` is checked only against the first sha. No current header has a range inside the parentheses in that shape. Fix: document it, or leave such a header unchecked.\n4. **Detail** — a reversed range (`:2-1`) is reported as \"range outside the file\". It is right to fail it, but the message is misleading.\n\nThe other two pointer edits are correct: `composerHeader` starts at `AnswerView.swift:765` @ 87fe0d1c. The README covers what round 1 asked for. The CI step runs in the Docs consistency job, which checks out with `fetch-depth: 0`.\n\n**Verified**: in a worktree at 6a63429: `python3 -m unittest discover scripts/tests` 211 OK; `check_legacy_pointers.py --fetch` 24 checked, 425 unchecked, 0 wrong; 24 parser probes (several `Port of` in one block, `@ sha and @ sha`, nested parentheses, CRLF, `Class.method`, `-foo:bar:`, `;` separators, `:0-2` and `:2-1`, `@sha` with no space, trailing `//`, `/* */`) with no false failure; legacy lines read at 87fe0d1c; SwiftLint on the edited file; markdownlint 0 errors; `git diff --check`.\n\nRound 2 fixed in 06ab060: the line is wrapped (`swiftlint lint --strict` on all of `App/` is now clean, no output); README says when `Class.method` is checked and that a two-sha header is checked against the first sha; a reversed range says « reversed range » (new test, 212 pass). Round 3 requested.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
