   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r3-opus-1252, round 3) : APPROVE** — head 06ab060\n\nAll three round-2 findings are fixed, and I found nothing new.\n\n1. Fixed: the `SeasonalDecorations.swift:3-5` line was too long. The longest line is now 127 characters, and `swiftlint lint --strict` passes. Nothing from the original comment is lost: \"setTheme `:382-388`\" became \"setTheme `:363-388`, the snow block at 382-388\". `git show 87fe0d1c:Classes/HFRplusAppDelegate.m` puts `-(void)setTheme:` at line 363 and the `snow` block at lines 382-388. The \"Differences (GAP-147)\" sentence is the same word for word; it only wraps to the next line.\n2. Fixed: the README gaps. `tooling/docs/README.md` now explains the `Class.method` rule (last component, camelCase or PascalCase, or in backticks). It also says a header with two shas is checked against the first only and is otherwise unchecked.\n3. Fixed: the reversed-range message. `check_legacy_pointers.py:149-151` reports \"reversed range\". `test_a_reversed_range_is_wrong_and_says_so` fails when I change that message, so the test holds (L01).\n\nAlso confirmed: `AnswerView.swift:765` at `87fe0d1c` is `private var composerHeader`, so the move from `:768-819` to `:765-819` in `ComposerHeader.swift` and `FloatingComposerButtons.swift` is correct.\n\n**Verified**\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` on all of `App/` (282 files): 0 errors. Also clean on the 3 changed Swift files.\n- `python3 -m unittest discover scripts/tests`: 212 tests OK.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/check_legacy_pointers.py --fetch`: 24 checked, 425 unchecked, 0 wrong, exit 0.\n- `npx markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1 tooling/docs/README.md`: 0 errors.\n- `git diff --check origin/dev-swift...HEAD`: clean.\n- The legacy line ranges read with `git show 87fe0d1c:…`, and the mutation probe on the reversed-range message.\n\nNot marked ready: the PR touches comments of 3 `App/` files, so its Compile check must be green first.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
